{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_022 (rna_only, scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is the current best at 0.5305 acc / 0.5152 F1, outperforming both multimodal+resnet50 configs (0.5121 concat, 0.5251 weighted). This strongly suggests RNA carries the dominant signal and resnet50 image features add noise. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (scgpt), so it is unclear whether the performance is driven by the learned scgpt representation or simply by the informativeness of the RNA data. Question: config_034 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) changes only the RNA encoder from scgpt to PCA while holding all other settings identical to config_022, cleanly isolating the RNA encoder effect. If PCA performs comparably to scgpt, the RNA signal is captured by linear structure and encoder choice is less critical; if PCA is substantially worse, scgpt's learned representation is essential. Why best next: This single-variable comparison resolves the most important open uncertainty (is scgpt special or is RNA just informative?) before investing budget in more complex multimodal or aggregation variants. The answer directly informs which RNA encoder to pair with image in future multimodal experiments, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

